# WolkaraForever layer patch 0063 - mobile interface: a drag around the spell wheel turns it
#
# Why: an installed interface (WolkaraRoue's iPhone Duo layout) can put a spell wheel in a
# ring around the screen's bottom-right corner. In combat the game lets an add-on move its
# spell buttons only in answer to a click or a mouse wheel, never to a drag, so a finger could
# not spin it in a fight. While the add-on's spinning wheel is on, it saves the ring its spells
# take (WolkaraRoueTouch: inner and outer edge, shares of the height, following its Reach and
# spell size); the touch controls publish that ring under WolkaraForeverSpellWheelV1, and a
# finger that comes down in it and moves is sent as wheel
# notches - one per 18 degrees of travel around the corner - with the pointer resting where
# the finger came down, which is where the wheel listens. A flick keeps turning for a moment
# after the finger lifts. A tap there is still a tap and a hold still a right click; only a
# drag changes. Each notch ticks the phone's haptics unless the touch controls' Haptics
# switch is off.
#
# Gated: direct touch in the mobile interface only, and only while the add-on has saved a ring
# (no ring without the spinning wheel, so no other interface or Fan style is affected).
#
# Applies to: translation/AppKit/AppKit.m (after 0055).
# Upstream: no.
#
diff --git a/translation/AppKit/AppKit.m b/translation/AppKit/AppKit.m
